course: dictionary
lesson: 2628
title: Desire: a strong wish
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A desire is a strong wish for something. As a noun you can write «Her desire was to find the lost treasure.» As a verb, which is more formal, you can write «She desired a quiet home by the sea.» Both mean that someone wants something very much.
explain: Read the words around desire to find its meaning. In «The boy had a burning desire to win», the word burning shows the wish is very strong. In «Their desire for friendship grew», the word for tells you what the wish is about.
explain: Watch out for the phrase «leave a lot to be desired». It does not mean that someone wants something. It means that the thing is not very good. «The school lunch left a lot to be desired» is a complaint: the lunch was poor.
explain: Writers sometimes say strong feelings and desires drive what we do. The philosopher Hume wrote, «Reason is the slave of the passions.» Here the passions are our strong feelings and desires, which set our goals, while reason helps us reach them. Try swapping in wish to check the meaning.
fact: Desire means a strong wish or longing for something.
fact: «Desire» can be a noun (a desire) or a verb (to desire, which is more formal).
fact: «A desire to» or «a desire for» is followed by what you want, such as «a desire for treasure».
fact: «The desired effect» means the result you wanted.
fact: «Leave a lot to be desired» means not very good.
exercise: «Her desire for a home by the sea grew each day.» What does desire mean here? | A bad smell | A loud noise | *A strong wish for something | A place to sleep
exercise: «The film was dull, and the plot left a lot to be desired.» What does this phrase suggest? | The film had no actors | *The film was not very good | The film was very long | The film was very good
exercise: «The sailors desired the treasure more than anything.» Find and copy the word that means wanted very much. | treasure | anything | sailors | *desired
test: «Our desire to win the match made us train hard.» What is the desire? | *A strong wish to win | A sore leg | A wish to lose | A new football
test: «The medicine gave the desired effect.» What does the desired effect mean? | *The result you wanted | A side effect nobody wanted | The end of the story | A empty bottle
exam: Ben says «desire» means the same as «dislike». Which is right? | *Ben is wrong, because a desire is a strong wish | Ben is right, desire means not liking | Desire means to be sleepy | Desire means to sing
